# The script the fixture harness runs stepped (`fixture-test`;
# docs/dev-practices/headless-mode.md, "How the gate runs a fixture") against
# the config in `config/`, which keeps the default layout, binds `C-c n` to
# a command that makes a buffer called `notes` and displays it, and makes
# one display rule, whose target, the right edge, the default layout
# lacks. It shows the rule left out at install and said, and a buffer a
# command opens that is not the one being edited, the buffer list and the
# command's, going to the stack while main keeps the buffer being edited.
# What it prints must be exactly `expected`. It touches no file.

# The report has a `rule:` line for the rule left out.
reload
settle

# A frame of 640 by 480: the tiled area is 640 by 464, above the bottom row.
# The echo area says the rule left out after `reload: `, and view 0 is
# alone.
resize 640 480
scene

# `draft` typed in insert state: the buffer being edited, `scratch`.
key i KeyI -
commit draft
key <Escape> Escape -

# `:ls` shows the buffer list in a new window at the end of the list, the
# stack, on the right, focused; main keeps `scratch`, showing `draft`.
key : Semicolon shift
commit ls
key <Enter> Enter -
scene

# `C-w h` focuses main, and `C-c n` puts `notes` in another new window at
# the end of the stack, below the list, focused; main is as it was.
key w KeyW control
key h KeyH -
key c KeyC control
key n KeyN -
scene

# `:ls` again, from `notes`: the list's window shows the list already, so it
# is focused, with the list brought up to date, naming `notes`; no window is
# made.
key : Semicolon shift
commit ls
key <Enter> Enter -
scene
